        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="has got">has got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="have got">have got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is got">is got</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Have you got" data-hint="The host must use the have-got question system with the subject you." data-fix="Have you got a reservation?">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. The host must use the have-got system to ask one guest about a reservation: ___ a reservation?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Have you got">Have you got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Has you got">Has you got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Are you got">Are you got</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="haven’t" data-hint="The subject we takes have, and very little time requires the negative haven't got." data-fix="We haven't got much time before the train leaves.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. The train leaves in five minutes, so the group has very little time. We ___ got much time.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="haven’t">haven’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="hasn’t">hasn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="don’t">don’t</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="hasn’t" data-hint="The prompt asks for a one-word short answer, so keep has, contract not, and omit got." data-fix="Has Leo got a car? No, he hasn't.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. Complete the negative short answer with one word: “Has Leo got a car?” “No, he ___.”</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="hasn’t">hasn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="hasn’t got">hasn’t got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="doesn’t">doesn’t</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="has" data-hint="Before got, the contraction she's expands to she has." data-fix="She's got means she has got, so 's means has.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. In the fictional profile “She’s got two brothers,” what does <span class="ex">’s</span> mean?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="has">has</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="does">does</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Do you have a car?" data-hint="The requested ordinary-have system uses do plus the base form have and contains no got." data-fix="Do you have a car? is the ordinary U.S. have question.">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. Which question correctly uses the ordinary U.S. <span class="ex">have</span> system?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do you have a car?">Do you have a car?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do you have got a car?">Do you have got a car?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Has you got a car?">Has you got a car?</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="has got" data-hint="The apartment is singular, and the listing uses the have-got system for one feature." data-fix="The apartment has got a balcony.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. A listing uses the have-got system to describe one apartment feature. The apartment ___ a balcony.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="has got">has got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="have got">have got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="got">got</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="’ve got" data-hint="The present condition belongs with I have got, contracted to I've got." data-fix="The fictional speaker says, 'I've got a headache today.'">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. A fictional speaker reports a present condition: “I ___ a headache today.”</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="’ve got">’ve got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="’s got">’s got</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="am got">am got</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
